---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 11, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — Envelope" description="Terms governing your use of Envelope.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 prose-envelope">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      By using Envelope you agree to these terms. This document is a draft and should be reviewed by counsel before launch.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Envelope provides budgeting software on iOS, Android, and the web. You may use the free tier or subscribe to Pro.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for keeping your account credentials secure and for all activity under your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not attempt to disrupt or reverse-engineer the service.</li>
      <li>Do not use Envelope for unlawful activity.</li>
      <li>Do not resell or redistribute access to the service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
    <p>
      Pro subscriptions renew automatically until cancelled. Cancel any time from your App Store, Google Play, or web account settings. Refunds are handled by the respective platform.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Envelope is provided "as is" without warranty. We are not financial advisors. Use the app to support your own decisions, not to replace professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, our liability is limited to the amount you paid us in the preceding twelve months.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced in-app or via email.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions? Email <a href="mailto:hello@envelope.app">hello@envelope.app</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
